WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.260
- There's sort of a mixed
story about pandemics.

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:06.960
You know Ebola and Zika, MERS and SARS,

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.770
Lassa fever, swine flu, bird flu.

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:13.040
There's been more animal viruses

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:14.970
jumping from animals to humans

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:16.870
in the last 30 years

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:19.230
than we have records of before,

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:21.083
and that's worrisome.

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:24.220
But much more worrisome than that

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:29.900
is that the institutions
that normally keep us safe

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:31.323
are sort of AWOL.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:34.233
In the Ebola outbreak,

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:41.400
Obama sent 3,500 American
soldiers to West Africa,

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:43.610
we spent billions of dollars,

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:48.070
because WHO failed in
its job to protect us,

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:50.700
'cause it took six months
to correctly identify

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:54.520
what the disease was that was
killing people in West Africa.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:58.360
So WHO is gonna have a new
director general in May

00:00:58.360 --> 00:00:59.390
and I think it's gonna go through

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:01.270
a period of self-examination,

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:03.023
and it's offline.

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:05.560
And I think this presidency,

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:08.410
as far as pandemics, is offline.

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:10.770
You're not gonna see public health,

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.950
let alone pandemic preparedness,

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:17.130
at the top of the priority
list for this White House.

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:19.090
And they fired the head of CDC

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:20.993
and they're cutting the budgets.

00:01:20.993 --> 00:01:22.520
- Center for Disease Control.

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:23.550
- Center for Disease Control,

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:26.173
or Centers for Disease Control, actually.

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:30.710
And Trump is cutting the budget

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:33.730
for public health and
pandemic preparedness.

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:35.770
There's a new secretary general of the UN

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:37.450
who just began on the first of January.

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:38.640
A really good guy,

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:40.450
Portuguese guy, really good,

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:42.530
but he's just getting started.

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:46.130
So if you look at those agencies
that normally keep us safe,

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:47.700
the federal government,

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:51.840
WHO, the UN, CDC,

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:53.510
they're all offline.

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:55.650
We've got a great head of the World Bank

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:57.623
who's a doctor, Jim Kim.

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:00.070
He'll be working really hard.

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:01.150
But by and large,

00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:05.760
we have to have a safety
net to protect us,

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:08.710
to stop pandemics, to end
the threat of pandemics.

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:11.530
April 7th is World Health Day.

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:16.240
It is also the 100th anniversary
of the Great Influenza,

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:21.240
the Spanish influenza,
the 1917 to 1918 pandemic.

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:23.780
One of my grandparents died in that,

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:25.700
one of Girija's grandparents died in it.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:29.630
I wonder how many other
people know that in your,

00:02:29.630 --> 00:02:32.340
you know, in your genealogy,

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:33.890
some of your relatives died from that.

00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:36.180
Because somewhere between 25 million

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:40.440
and a hundred million people
died in that one year period.

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:42.940
And if you put that to today's numbers,

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:45.423
you're talking about 75 to 300 million.

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:50.270
If we had a pandemic 1/10th
of that, 1/100th of that,

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:52.480
it would bring humanity to its knees.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:55.500
There wouldn't be an airplane
in the sky for six months.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:59.020
Who's gonna get on a
cargo boat with 300 people

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:02.130
whose epidemiological
status you don't know

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:05.770
when there's no vaccine and no antiviral?

00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:09.370
I want us to stop the risk of pandemics.

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:10.720
We know almost every,

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:12.780
well, we know every step to take.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:14.490
We know how to do it.

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:16.220
There will inevitably be outbreaks.

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:19.750
There'll be viruses jumping
from animals to humans.

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:21.240
Outbreaks are inevitable,

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:22.683
but pandemics are optional.

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:25.300
We don't have to have them

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:28.410
if we have the same
public will to end them

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:30.530
that we had to eradicate smallpox

00:03:30.530 --> 00:03:32.989
and that's what I'm hoping
that we can pull off next.

